==============================================================================
STEP 4 -- THE COUPLING THE EXACT LANDING NEEDS IS OUTSIDE QED'S RANGE
==============================================================================
  landing the anchor exactly on 4 pi m_H needs   1/alpha = 140.74   (alpha_c = 0.021316)
  the corpus records this as 140.7 / 0.021316

  but the running coupling is bounded ABOVE by its zero-momentum value:
    1/alpha(0)  = 137.036   <- the largest 1/alpha QED ever takes
    1/alpha needed = 140.74
    gap = 3.70 in 1/alpha, i.e. 2.70% weaker than the infrared limit

  Running takes alpha the other way -- stronger in the ultraviolet, so 1/alpha only
  falls as the scale rises. The value the exact landing wants is therefore attained at
  NO scale whatever, which is a stronger statement than 'the wrong scale was chosen'.
  The best case available anywhere is the infrared endpoint, and there the anchor
  overshoots 4 pi m_H by x2.003 -- which is the factor the chain is actually carrying.
